  <!-- Application -->
  <h2 id="application">Application</h2>

  <p>The food and other process industries use the 3-phase decanter extensively. The primary application is to separate a feed slurry of two immiscible liquids and a solid phase.</p>

  <p>A typical example would be separating an oil phase from the water and solids phase.</p>

  <p>Oilfield service is the clearest case. In a <a href="/crude-oil-tank-bottom-recovery-centrifuge/">tank bottom recovery</a> or refinery slop oil train, the three phase decanter is the front-end machine: it takes the raw emulsion and splits recovered sale oil, water, and sand in one pass, so the disc stack centrifuge downstream only has to polish clean oil. Dolphin supplies these as remanufactured Alfa Laval UVNX 314 and UVNX 418 decanters, skid-mounted or containerized for remote sites, with US engineering support and startup from Warren, Michigan.</p>

  <p>Other specific examples include:</p>

  <ul>
    <li><a href="/crude-oil-tank-bottom-recovery-centrifuge/">Crude Oil Separation</a> from Water and Sludge</li>
    <li><a href="/disc-stack-centrifuge-applications/">Fish Oil Separation</a> from Stickwater and Fish Meal</li>
    <li><a href="/wastewater-centrifuge/">Industrial Waste Water</a> from Oil and Sludge</li>
    <li>Beef Tallow from Water &amp; Solids</li>
  </ul>

